# ROADMAP — Release Pin, Rebuild & Multi-Agent Staged Sprint Plan

File: openOODA/ROADMAP.oot
Active sprint plan, rebuild verification gates, and feature milestone locks.
All engineering execution aligns with the 6 Strategic Pillars, Boyd's E-M performance engine, and Power Law 80/20 leverage.
This board is the plan. Proof of completion lives in SHIPPED.oot (produced by `scripts/generate_shipped.oo`).

## 1. Release Pin & State

Release: v0.211.5. Product libraries: `ooda/std`. GitHub `openOODA/std` archived.
Product tip (ooda): main. Boards tip: main.
Named emit+gcc+run still required. A folder on disk is not a volume certification.
Live pin, timings, and backend locks: SHIPPED.oot after `scripts/generate_shipped.oo`.

## 2. Rebuild Velocity (Pillar 2 Boyd's E-M Performance Engine)

Microsecond rebuild velocity ($V$) is verified through the pure self-hosted bootstrap:
From `ooda/`:
  export PURE_NO_ARC=0
  OODAC_BIN=./bootstrap/seed/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
  OODAC_BIN=./oodac/oodac bash bootstrap/oodac_pure_build oodac/main.oo oodac/oodac
  ./oodac/oodac check oodac/main.oo
Official rebuild is `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`. `PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1` is opt-in only.

## 3. Status Vocabulary

- `done` — Works, proved on disk by a named lock.
- `smoke` — Small verification check passes cleanly.
- `partial` — Partially implemented and compiling.
- `residual` — Wanted in NORTHSTAR or MOONSHOTS, not yet built.
- `open` — In progress during active multi-agent sprint.
- `stale` — Leftover words; a later proof closed them.

## 4. Product Path & Strategic Pillars Alignment

- Product Path: C emit + gcc + `chs_rt` runtime is the primary product path.
- Pillar 1 (First Principles): Derive AST nodes and compiler transforms directly from hardware invariants and RFCs.
- Pillar 2 (Boyd's E-M Engine): $E-M = ((T - D) / W) \cdot V$. Maximize instruction thrust ($T$), eliminate ARC/heap drag ($D$), minimize binary weight ($W$), and accelerate rebuild velocity ($V$).
- Pillar 3 (Adversarial Validation): All features must pass the sequential Double-Run execution law (`./bin/ooda run <test.oo>`) in fresh processes.
- Pillar 4 (Power Law 80/20): Concentrate compiler architecture on high-leverage primitives (SSA mem2reg, flat closures, direct ELF64 emission, linear arena memory).
- Pillar 5 (Blue Ocean Strategy): Defend zero ambient authority capability security model and zero-toolchain self-bootstrapping.
- Pillar 6 (Multi-Agent Swarm Protocol): Coordinate multi-agent development with continuous git awareness and non-clobbering integration.

## 5. Active Sprint: Staged Backend Execution Plan

Each feature row requires a named smoke lock. A checked box is not proof; re-run the smoke test.
A feature is certified only when its row's smoke passes on both `emit-x86` (token path) and `emit-x86-ssa` (SSA path) under double-run execution.

### 5.1 x86 Backend Staged Plan (Per-Language-Feature)

#### Phase A — Foundation (Tier 5)
- [ ] Tier 5 #24 — RFC 0011: AST-based pipeline using std/arch_x86/x86_codegen.oo → `scripts/x86_ast_typed_smoke.oo` [RFC 0011]
- [ ] Tier 5 #25 — mem2reg + ssa_opt wired in x86_ssa_compile.oo → `scripts/x86_ssa_opt_smoke.oo`
- [ ] Tier 5 #26 — per-block register remap in x86_ssa_emit.oo → `scripts/x86_ssa_block_remap_smoke.oo`
- [ ] Tier 5 #27 — delete 22-token-matcher ladder in x86_emit.oo → `scripts/x86_no_template_smoke.oo` [RFC 0011]

#### Phase B — Language Features (Per-Feature)
- [ ] **Int** println (basic Int arg, signed Int arg, simple Int arith) → `scripts/x86_ssa_int_smoke.oo` + `scripts/x86_int_smoke.oo` (passes)
- [ ] **Float** IEEE-754 arith (real, not hardcoded x*y+1.0) → `scripts/x86_ssa_float_runtime_smoke.oo` + `scripts/x86_ssa_float_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **String** println of literal → `scripts/x86_ssa_string_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **List[T]** list_new/list_push/list_get/list_set/list_len → `scripts/x86_ssa_list_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **Struct** field init + field read + field write → `scripts/x86_ssa_struct_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **Option/Result** 2-8 arm match → `scripts/x86_ssa_match_smoke.oo` (3-arm minimum)
- [ ] **While** 6 OPs (< <= > >= == !=) → `scripts/x86_while_general_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **For** for x in 0..N → `scripts/x86_for_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **Function call** 1-6 arg SysV → `scripts/x86_ssa_call_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **Bitwise** & | ^ << >> → `scripts/x86_bitwise_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **Capability** &SysCap, &FsCap, &AllocCap, &ThreadCap → `scripts/x86_cap_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **Contract** requires/ensures/spec/verify → `scripts/x86_ssa_contract_smoke.oo`
- [ ] **SECRET** taint on 6 sinks → `scripts/x86_ssa_secret_smoke.oo`

#### Phase C — Production Glue (Tier 6/7)
- [ ] Tier 6 #29 — multi-file emit → `scripts/x86_ssa_multi_smoke.oo` [RFC 0012]
- [ ] Tier 6 #31 — typed error reporter (--> , ^) → `scripts/x86_diag_smoke.oo`
- [ ] Tier 7 #32 — `--x86-elf-pure` CLI flag → `scripts/x86_direct_elf_smoke.oo`
- [ ] Tier 7 #33 — x86 runtime registry consolidation → `scripts/x86_runtime_registry_smoke.oo`
- [ ] Tier 7 #34 — bit-identical reproducibility → `scripts/x86_bit_identical_smoke.oo`

#### Phase D — Parallel Backends (AArch64)
- [ ] AArch64 0-matcher gap closure (Tier 0 in audit/aarch64-investigations.oot) → reuses audit/aarch64-investigations.oot §6 plan
- [ ] Deprecate hand-written GAS path; call std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_codegen.oo directly

#### Phase E — Quality (Tier 8/9)
- [ ] Tier 8 #35 — Academy headers (keep `dinner_lint` running)
- [ ] Tier 8 #36 — dinner_lint clean
- [ ] Tier 8 #39 — convert all 88 x86 fixtures + 76 smokes to AST-based regression
- [ ] Tier 8 #42 — AArch64 parallel investigation complete
- [ ] Tier 9 #45 — C-vs-x86 run parity smoke
- [ ] Tier 9 #46 — SIMD smoke (mulsd/addsd/subsd/divsd on battery of FP inputs)
- [ ] Tier 9 #47 — threads/capability smoke (real ThreadCap/AllocCap wiring)
- [ ] Tier 9 #50 — bit-identical cross-host smoke

Out of scope until later: full general symbolic SMT, hardware enclaves (SGX/TDX/SEV), device GPU dispatch, browser WASM host. C emit + gcc + chs_rt stays the everyday product path.

### 5.2 AArch64 Backend Staged Plan (Per-Language-Feature)

Plan and analysis: `audit/aarch64-investigations.oot`. AArch64 features 0% silent-miscompile by static analysis.
The std-level `std/arch_aarch64/aarch64_codegen.oo` is wired into `aarch64_emit_elf.oo`.

Tier 0 — Close 0-matcher gap across all emit modules — refuse-don't-miscompile.
Tier 1 — Deprecate hand-written GAS path in `aarch64_emit_sys.oo`; call `aarch64_compile_to_elf` directly.
Tier 2 — Host probe: `qemu-aarch64 -L /usr/aarch64-linux-gnu ./a.bin` on 53 fixtures.
Tier 3 — Move 53 aarch64 fixtures to `ooda/fixtures-aarch64/`.
Tier 4 — Close 0-matcher gap to documented ladder.

Out of scope: device GPU dispatch, hardware enclaves, browser WASM, full general symbolic SMT.

